      'When a firm receives a large block order from an institutional client, the firm cannot front-run the order by placing a firm\'s orders ahead of the block.\n\nTrading Ahead of Research Reports\n\nIf a firm\'s research department is going to issue a report on a company that is likely to affect the price of its stock, the firm cannot trade based on advance knowledge of the recommendation. Once the recommendation is disseminated, the firm is not bound by this restriction.\n\nActing as Both Broker and Dealer for the Same Trade\n\nFINRA prohibits a firm from acting as both an agent and principal in a single transaction. When a firm acts as a broker or agent, they charge a commission to match a buyer with a seller. When a firm acts as a dealer or principal on a trade, they will not charge a commission but will mark up or mark down the price. A firm cannot charge a commission and a markup/markdown on the same transaction.',
